===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|countee}}, {{m|enm|counte}}, {{m|enm|conte}}, from {{der|en|xno|counté}}, {{der|en|fro|conté}} (French {{m|fr|comté}}), from {{der|en|la|comitātus||jurisdiction of a count}}, from {{m|la|comes||count, earl}}. Cognate with {{cog|es|condado||county}} and {{cog|it|contea||county}}. {{doublet|en|comitatus}}, borrowed directly from Latin. Mostly displaced native {{ncog|ang|sċīr}}, whence {{w|Modern English}} {{m|en|shire}}.

